            <ArticleTitle>Acute non-traumatic spinal subdural haematoma: an unusual aetiology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>842-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jocn.2008.09.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an unusual case of a spinal subdural haematoma associated with a ruptured spinal aneurysm. The delayed diagnosis or misdiagnosis of this rare entity can have disastrous consequences. We discuss various possible aetiologies and its association with spinal aneurysms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
